 "AudioStream": "## AudioStream — Plays audio samples the logic produces, in real time.\nTag: <AudioStream> (group: media)\nProps (? = optional):\n- getSamples?: function — Called when the scheduler needs more audio. Receives the number of frames that would fill the lead buffer, and returns either a base64 string of interleaved PCM, an {@link AudioStreamBlock}, or `null`/`undefined` for \"nothing right now\". Returning nothing is a normal, cheap answer — the component simply asks again — and is the right answer when the producer has no samples ready. Do not pad with silence: silence inserted mid-stream lands as a click, whereas a short queue does not. May be synchronous or return a promise; script functions running in a worker are asynchronous and are awaited. Called on the component's own schedule, driven by how far ahead the queue runs — not on a frame timer. It keeps running while the tab is in the background, where `requestAnimationFrame` does not.\n- sampleRate?: number — Rate to ask the audio system for, in Hz (default 48000). A request, not a promise: the browser and the output device both get a say, and Safari refuses rates it cannot do natively rather than resampling. `onReady` reports the rate actually in use, and a producer should generate at that rate rather than assume this one.\n- channels?: 1 | 2 — Channels in the PCM the producer will send: 1 or 2 (default 2)\n- format?: PcmFormat — Sample format of the PCM (default 'i16' — signed 16-bit, little-endian)\n- bufferMs?: number — Target lead buffer in milliseconds (default 80). The queue is kept roughly this far ahead of the playhead. Larger is safer — it is how much main-thread stall the stream survives without a gap — and smaller is more responsive, which matters when the audio answers an input. 80ms survives an ordinary garbage collection; below about 30ms an unlucky layout is audible.\n- running?: boolean — Whether the stream is pulling audio (default true)\n- muted?: boolean — Silence the output without stopping the stream (default false)\n- volume?: number — Output gain, 0..1 (default 1)\n- showControls?: boolean — Show the built-in status strip and the unlock button (default true)\n- unlockLabel?: string — Label on the button shown while the browser is blocking audio\n- children?: node — Rendered below the status strip\nEvents (write @name={…}; the prop is onName):\n- @ready — Called once the graph is actually running, with the real context rate. This is the moment a producer should configure itself: until it has fired there is no audio clock to match. The second argument carries the rest of the graph's shape for producers that need it.\n- @underrun — Called when the queue starves, at most a few times a second\n- @error — Called when the audio graph cannot be built\nChildren: accepts child content.\nEvery component also takes style and className.\nMinimal usage: <AudioStream>…</AudioStream>",
 "Avatar": "## Avatar — A person's picture, or their initials when there is none.\nTag: <Avatar> (group: minimal)\nProps (? = optional):\n- src?: string — Image source\n- alt?: string — Alt text\n- name?: string — User name (for initials fallback)\n- size?: 'xs' | 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' | 'xl' | number — Avatar size\n- shape?: \"circle\" | \"square\" | \"rounded\" — Avatar shape\n- border?: boolean — Border\n- borderColor?: string — Border color\n- backgroundColor?: string — Background color (for initials)\n- textColor?: string — Text color (for initials)\n- status?: \"online\" | \"offline\" | \"away\" | \"busy\" | \"none\" — Online status indicator\n- statusPosition?: \"top-right\" | \"bottom-right\" | \"top-left\" | \"bottom-left\" — Status position\n- badge?: string | number — Badge content (number or text)\n- badgeColor?: string — Badge color\n- ring?: boolean — Show ring on hover\n- ringColor?: string — Ring color\n- ariaLabel?: string — Accessible label (for interactive avatars)\n- children?: node — Children (for custom content)\nEvents (write @name={…}; the prop is onName):\n- @click — Click handler\n- @keyDown — Keyboard handler\nChildren: accepts child content.\nEvery component also takes style and className.\nMinimal usage: <Avatar>…</Avatar>",
