 "Badge": "## Badge — A small count or status label.\nTag: <Badge> (group: minimal)\nProps (? = optional):\n- variant?: \"default\" | \"primary\" | \"secondary\" | \"success\" | \"warning\" | \"danger\" | \"info\" — Badge variant\n- badgeStyle?: \"solid\" | \"subtle\" | \"outline\" — Badge style\n- size?: \"xs\" | \"sm\" | \"md\" | \"lg\" — Badge size\n- pill?: boolean — Whether it's a pill shape\n- dot?: boolean — Whether it's just a dot\n- content?: string | number — Content (number or text)\n- max?: number — Maximum count (for numbers)\n- leftIcon?: node — Left icon\n- rightIcon?: node — Right icon\n- pulse?: boolean — Pulse animation (for notifications)\n- glow?: boolean — Glow effect\n- children?: node — Children\nChildren: accepts child content.\nEvery component also takes style and className.\nMinimal usage: <Badge>…</Badge>",
 "BarChart": "## BarChart — Vertical or horizontal bar chart; grouped or stacked series.\nTag: <BarChart> (group: charts)\nProps (? = optional):\n- series: BarChartSeries[]\n- width?: number\n- height?: number\n- padding?: { top: number; right: number; bottom: number; left: number }\n- orientation?: \"vertical\" | \"horizontal\"\n- grouped?: boolean\n- stacked?: boolean\n- barPadding?: number\n- groupPadding?: number\n- showGrid?: boolean\n- showValues?: boolean\n- showLegend?: boolean\n- formatValue?: function\n- interactive?: boolean\n- ariaLabel?: string — Text alternative for the chart; a summary of its values by default\nTypes the props use:\n- BarChartSeries = { name: string; data: BarDataPoint[]; color?: string }\n- BarDataPoint = { label: string; value: number; color?: string }\nChildren: none (configure it with props).\nEvery component also takes style and className.\nMinimal usage: <BarChart series={[]} />",
 "Box": "## Box — A plain box with padding, background, border, radius and shadow props.\nTag: <Box> (group: minimal)\nProps (? = optional):\n- padding?: 'none' | 'xs' | 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' | 'xl' | string — Padding\n- margin?: 'none' | 'xs' | 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' | 'xl' | string — Margin\n- background?: string — Background color\n- borderRadius?: 'none' | 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' | 'full' | string — Border radius\n- border?: string — Border\n- shadow?: 'none' | 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' | 'xl' | string — Shadow\n- flex?: number | string — Flex value\n- overflow?: \"visible\" | \"hidden\" | \"scroll\" | \"auto\" — Overflow\n- width?: string — Width\n- height?: string — Height\n- minWidth?: string — Min width\n- minHeight?: string — Min height\n- maxWidth?: string — Max width\n- maxHeight?: string — Max height\n- children?: node — Children\nEvents (write @name={…}; the prop is onName):\n- @click — Click handler\n- @keyDown — Keyboard handler\n- @pointerDown — Pointer handlers, forwarded to the element. A template binds them as `@pointerdown` / `@pointerup` / `@pointermove` / `@pointercancel` / `@pointerleave`, which is how an app gets a press-and-release pair or a swipe out of a plain box. None of them make the box focusable or give it a button role; only `onClick` does that.\n- @pointerUp\n- @pointerMove\n- @pointerCancel\n- @pointerLeave\n- @contextMenu — Context-menu handler; a hold-to-press control uses it to swallow the long-press menu.\nChildren: accepts child content.\nEvery component also takes style and className.\nMinimal usage: <Box>…</Box>",
