 "Button": "## Button — A clickable button: variants, sizes, loading and disabled states.\nTag: <Button> (group: minimal)\nProps (? = optional):\n- type?: \"button\" | \"submit\" | \"reset\" — Button type\n- variant?: \"primary\" | \"secondary\" | \"outline\" | \"danger\" | \"success\" | \"warning\" | \"ghost\" | \"link\" — Button variant\n- size?: \"xs\" | \"sm\" | \"md\" | \"lg\" | \"xl\" — Button size\n- disabled?: boolean — Whether the button is disabled\n- loading?: boolean — Whether the button is loading\n- fullWidth?: boolean — Full width\n- rounded?: boolean — Rounded style (pill shape)\n- iconOnly?: boolean — Icon only button (square aspect ratio)\n- leftIcon?: node — Left icon\n- rightIcon?: node — Right icon\n- ariaLabel?: string — Accessible name. Required in practice for `iconOnly` buttons and for any button whose whole label is a glyph — a screen reader reads \"+\" as nothing useful, and until this existed there was no way for a template to say what such a button does.\n- aria-label?: string — Alias, for hosts that pass DOM attribute names straight through.\n- title?: string — Native tooltip.\n- children?: node — Children\nEvents (write @name={…}; the prop is onName):\n- @click — Click handler\n- @pointerDown — Pointer handlers, forwarded to the element. `onClick` fires on release; a control that has to know about the press itself (an emulator's A button, held through a jump) binds `@pointerdown` and `@pointerup` too.\n- @pointerUp\n- @pointerCancel\n- @pointerLeave\n- @contextMenu — Context-menu handler; a hold-to-press control swallows the long-press menu with it.\nChildren: accepts child content.\nEvery component also takes style and className.\nMinimal usage: <Button>…</Button>\nFrom the docs (first-app):\n```xml\n<Button @click={() => reset()}>Reset</Button>\n```",
 "Camera": "## Camera — Live camera view that can capture a photo or video (needs the camera permission).\nTag: <Camera> (group: media)\nProps (? = optional):\n- mode?: \"photo\" | \"video\" | \"live\" — Operating mode (default 'photo')\n- facing?: \"user\" | \"environment\" — Camera facing mode (default 'user')\n- width?: number — Video width in pixels (default 640)\n- height?: number — Video height in pixels (default 480)\n- frameRate?: number — Frame rate for live mode, in fps (default 10)\n- quality?: number — JPEG quality 0-1 (default 0.7)\n- active?: boolean — Whether the camera is active (default true)\n- audio?: boolean — Whether to capture sound as well as pictures (default: true in `video` mode, false otherwise). Sound is the microphone, which is its own capability: a bundle that declares `camera` alone gets silent video, and one that wants a soundtrack declares `mic` too.\n- showControls?: boolean — Whether to show built-in controls (default true)\n- children?: node — Children rendered as overlay\nEvents (write @name={…}; the prop is onName):\n- @capture — Called when a photo is captured\n- @frame — Called on each live frame\n- @record — Called when video recording completes\n- @error — Called when an error occurs\nChildren: accepts child content.\nEvery component also takes style and className.\nMinimal usage: <Camera>…</Camera>",
 "Card": "## Card — A bordered or elevated panel, with an optional title and subtitle.\nTag: <Card> (group: minimal)\nProps (? = optional):\n- title?: string — Card title (shown in header)\n- subtitle?: string — Card subtitle\n- variant?: \"default\" | \"outlined\" | \"elevated\" | \"filled\" | \"ghost\" | \"glass\" | \"gradient\" — Card variant\n- padding?: 'none' | 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' | 'xl' | string — Padding\n- borderRadius?: 'none' | 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg' | 'xl' | string — Border radius\n- hover?: boolean — Whether the card is interactive (hoverable) - shorthand for interactive\n- interactive?: boolean — Whether the card is interactive (hoverable)\n- selected?: boolean — Whether the card is selected\n- gradientFrom?: string — Gradient background colors (for gradient variant)\n- gradientTo?: string\n- header?: node — Header content (replaces title)\n- footer?: node — Footer content\n- headerActions?: node — Header actions (right side of header)\n- dividers?: boolean — Whether to show dividers\n- children?: node — Children\nEvents (write @name={…}; the prop is onName):\n- @click — Click handler (makes card interactive)\n- @keyDown — Keyboard handler\nChildren: accepts child content.\nEvery component also takes style and className.\nMinimal usage: <Card>…</Card>",
