 "DPad": "## DPad — An on-screen directional pad for games: press and release per direction.\nTag: <DPad> (group: minimal)\nAn on-screen directional pad. Each direction is held, not clicked: `onPress` when a pointer or key goes down, `onRelease` when it comes up. A release is sent once per press — and also when the pointer is cancelled, leaves the button while pressed, the button loses focus, or the pad unmounts — so a character is never left walking. Enter and Space hold a focused direction like a pointer does.\nProps (? = optional):\n- buttonSize?: number\n- color?: string\n- visible?: boolean\n- ariaLabel?: string — Accessible name for the pad as a whole\nEvents (write @name={…}; the prop is onName):\n- @press\n- @release\nChildren: none (configure it with props).\nEvery component also takes style and className.\nMinimal usage: <DPad />",
 "Draggable": "## Draggable — Makes its children draggable within bounds.\nTag: <Draggable> (group: animation)\nProps (? = optional):\n- axis?: \"both\" | \"x\" | \"y\" — Constrain drag axis\n- bounds?: 'parent' | DragBounds — Constrain drag to parent element or fixed bounds\n- disabled?: boolean — Disable dragging\n- grid?: number — Snap to grid interval in pixels\n- children: node — Content to make draggable\nTypes the props use:\n- DragBounds = { top: number; right: number; bottom: number; left: number }\nEvents (write @name={…}; the prop is onName):\n- @dragStart — Callback when dragging starts\n- @drag — Callback during dragging\n- @dragEnd — Callback when dragging ends\nChildren: accepts child content.\nEvery component also takes style and className.\nMinimal usage: <Draggable>…</Draggable>",
